help them lead a successful life in the United States. Learning acculturation and really understand how you do that is really an important process of our learning curve and addressing immigrants. We've spoken a lot during this conversation about trauma and I want to turn to the subject of resilience. So you're involved. in a report with APA's immigration working group. You published a paper called Vulnerable but but not broken and that was about the psychosocial challenges and resilience among unaccompanied minors from Central America. So in an interview you did with the Monitor article for the September 2019 issue, you explained how important it is to publish this report
